>> title: Chewy Granola Bars
>> category: Bars & Brownies
>> tags: oats, honey, snack, dessert, oven
>> counters: Bakery
>> aka: granola bar, muesli bar, oat and honey bar
>> servings: 9
>> time: 2 hr 30 min
>> slack: narrow — stirred over the heat the mixture toasts the oats and sets hard instead of chewy, and once it is pressed into the tin the texture is decided

Preheat the #oven{} to 350°F (175°C).

Line an #8x8-in pan{} with parchment, leaving an overhang on two sides.

Toast @rolled oats{2%cup}(180 g), @raw sunflower seeds{1/4%cup}(35 g) on a #sheet pan{} at 350°F for ~{10%min}.

Simmer @honey{1/3%cup}(115 g), @light brown sugar{1/4%cup}(50 g), @unsalted butter{3%Tbs}(42 g), @table salt{1/4%tsp}(1.5 g) in a #saucepan{} for ~{2%min}.

>> step: stir everything together off the heat
Off the heat, stir @&(~2)toasted oats{} into @&(~1)honey syrup{} with @crisp rice cereal{1%cup}(30 g), @dried cranberries{1/2%cup}(60 g), @mini chocolate chips{1/3%cup}(60 g).

Press @&(~1)granola mixture{} hard into the pan, then chill ~{2%hr}.
